# Julia versions CI passes to setup-julia. One version per line.
# Write the version itself (1.13, ~1.14.0-0, nightly). Do not use min / max.
# The stable line and `nightly` use that string as the job title.
# `~1.14.0-0` is the version string; the job title says `1.14-pre`.
# When a required version changes, change those job names and the main
# ruleset in that PR. The first version line is the E2E default, so
# `~1.14.0-0` stays below `1.13`.
#
# First stable line: maintained stable, Project.toml julia floor. Required.
#   Pkg.test, Aqua, JETLS, Documenter, bake, E2E kit parent, GHCR worker.
# `~1.14.0-0`: 1.14.0 prereleases (alpha, then beta, then rc, then 1.14.0).
#   It does not move to 1.15. continue-on-error.
#   Ubuntu Pkg.test, Aqua, and JETLS on heavy PRs, including ordinary PRs,
#   and on main, CI weekly, and a version cut.
#   macOS and WSL2 on CI weekly only.
#   No E2E or docs. Do not add another stable line.
# `nightly` (Julia master): continue-on-error. No JETLS.
#   Ubuntu Pkg.test and Aqua on main, CI weekly, and a version cut.
#   macOS and WSL2 on CI weekly only.
#   No E2E or docs.
#
# The required JETLS job uses the stable line. The tip line also runs JETLS.
1.13
~1.14.0-0
nightly
# E2E mismatch only (setup --juliaup). Not a test version.
JULIA_E2E_MISMATCH_CHANNEL=1.12
